      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Create and use layout pages, sections, and partial views for consistent UI structure."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Scenario:** Configure or implement the described functionality in an ASP.NET Core application."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Approach 1: Layout Pages and Sections"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Define a shared layout with RenderBody and RenderSection to structure the page."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Layout Pages and Sections",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "<!-- Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml -->\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>@ViewData[\"Title\"] - MyApp</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"~/css/site.css\" />\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <nav>@await Html.PartialAsync(\"_Navbar\")</nav>\n    </header>\n    <main role=\"main\" class=\"container\">\n        @RenderBody()\n    </main>\n    <footer>\n        @RenderSection(\"Scripts\", required: false)\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n\n<!-- Usage in view -->\n@{ Layout = \"_Layout\"; ViewData[\"Title\"] = \"Home\"; }\n<h2>Welcome</h2>\n@section Scripts {\n    <script src=\"~/js/home.js\"></script>\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Approach 2: View Start and View Import"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use _ViewStart.cshtml for common view logic and _ViewImports.cshtml for common directives."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "View Start and View Import",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "<!-- Views/_ViewStart.cshtml -->\n@{ Layout = \"_Layout\"; }\n\n<!-- Views/_ViewImports.cshtml -->\n@using MyApp.Models\n@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers\n\n<!-- Now any view automatically gets the layout -->\n<h2>About Us</h2>\n<p>No need to set Layout manually.</p>"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "comparison-cards",
      "data": {
        "title": "Approach Comparison",
        "cards": [
          {
            "title": "Layout Pages and Sections",
            "description": "Shared layout with sections",
            "pros": [
              "Consistent UI across pages",
              "Sections for page-specific scripts",
              "Easy to update globally"
            ],
            "cons": ["Nested layouts can be confusing", "Section names must match exactly"],
            "tags": ["_Layout", "RenderBody()", "RenderSection()"]
          },
          {
            "title": "View Start and View Import",
            "description": "Auto-apply layout and imports",
            "pros": ["No repetition", "All views inherit layout", "Common directives in one place"],
            "cons": ["Can hide important configuration", "Applies to all views in folder"],
            "tags": ["_ViewStart", "_ViewImports", "@addTagHelper"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
